PROVEN_BY_REASONING  sliding-window-phantom-index                  The single drain holder reads nextIndex == size-1, so the loop condition passes. Cancellation wins settled and executes nextIndex.getAndSet(size). The holder's getAndIncrement() returns size and stores size+1. Without handoff's index >= size guard, tasks.get(size) is out of bounds. draining admits one claimant, normal claims stop at size, and only the winning cancellation performs getAndSet, so the phantom index is exactly size.
